ODIN (Open Droid INterface) is dual-licensed by the kind of material:

  Hardware   CERN-OHL-S-2.0   see LICENSE-HARDWARE
  Software   MIT              see LICENSE-SOFTWARE

"Hardware" means the hardware design source: schematics, PCB layouts,
footprints, symbols, enclosure and mechanical designs, and the scripts
that generate them.

"Software" means firmware, host tools, the browser-based editor, the
Cyphal DSDL definitions, and any other source code not covered above.

Where a file carries its own SPDX-License-Identifier header, that header
takes precedence for that file.

SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0 AND MIT
